@startuml
' REVIEWED_MAIN_2026_05_13: aligned to current merged code; large-investment retained pending simplification merge.

title Why Two Signatures? — Off-Chain Payload (Broken) vs On-Chain Proposal (Standard)

skinparam maxMessageSize 280
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
autonumber

box "Environment A (Dirty / Untrusted)" #LightPink
actor "Initiator" as Init
participant "Squads Web UI\n(Compromisable)" as UI
end box

box "Out-of-Band" #White
participant "Secure Channel\n(Slack / Signal)" as OOB
end box

box "Environment B (Secure / Clean)" #LightGreen
actor "Approver 1" as Ap1
actor "Approver 2" as Ap2
actor "Approver 3" as Ap3
participant "HW Wallet\n(Clear-Signing Device)" as HW
end box

box "Infrastructure" #LightBlue
participant "Private RPC" as RPC
database "Solana Mainnet\n(Squads V4)" as Squads
end box

== BROKEN: Off-Chain "Pass the TXID" Approach ==

note over Init, Squads #Salmon
  **Hypothesis:** Skip the on-chain proposal. Build the TX off-chain,
  send a TXID/hash to the Approver, and let them sign just once.
  **Result:** This breaks down for 4 fundamental reasons.
end note

Init -> UI: Build transaction payload off-chain
note right of UI: TX stays off-chain.\nNo on-chain record exists yet.
UI --> Init: Raw TX bytes + hash (TXID)

Init -> OOB: "Check TXID: 7xF3...9aB2\nIntent: Safe Protocol Upgrade"
OOB -> Ap1: Receives TXID hash + intent

note over Ap1, HW #Salmon
  **FAILURE 1 — The TXID Problem**
  HW Wallet receives a hash (7xF3...9aB2).
  It **cannot decode a hash into human-readable text**.
  To display "Upgrade Program to <addr>", the HW needs
  the **entire raw instruction byte array**, not a hash.

  The hash is opaque — approver is blind-signing.
end note

Ap1 ->x HW: Pass TXID hash?\nHW screen: "Sign unknown data: 7xF3...9aB2"

note over Init, OOB #Salmon
  **FAILURE 2 — Transport Problem**
  Since proposal doesn't exist on-chain, you must pass
  the **full raw byte payload** (not an index) via OOB.
  Complex Squads V4 instructions can be hundreds of bytes.

  Options: massive QR code, Bluetooth, or copy-paste
  a giant Base64 string into Slack.
  **Terrible UX. Highly error-prone.**
end note

Init ->x OOB: Pass entire raw TX payload via Slack?\n"AQAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAABh\nFw8DAAAAAQAAAAMAAAA..."
note right of OOB #Salmon: Hundreds of bytes.\nTransport errors likely.\nNot human-verifiable.

note over Ap1, Ap3 #Salmon
  **FAILURE 3 — Solana TX Size Limit (1232 bytes)**
  Complex multisig actions (e.g., program upgrade with
  7 signers) may exceed the 1232-byte transaction limit
  if instructions + signatures are packed in one TX.

  Squads V4 solves this by storing instructions in a PDA
  on-chain first — which requires the Initiator to sign
  CreateTransaction and pay ~0.002 SOL rent.
end note

note over Ap1, Ap3 #Salmon
  **FAILURE 4 — Threshold Coordination (M-of-N)**
  With 3-of-5 threshold and no on-chain proposal:
  Ap1 signs raw payload → sends to Ap2 → Ap2 signs →
  sends to Ap3 → Ap3 signs → broadcasts.

  **Sequential relay of partially-signed payloads.**
  Logistical nightmare. No async voting.
  Each approver must trust the relay chain.
end note

Ap1 ->x Ap2: Forward partially-signed payload?
Ap2 ->x Ap3: Forward again?
note over Ap3 #Salmon: Cannot verify payload\nhasn't been swapped in transit.

|||

== STANDARD: On-Chain Proposal via Squads V4 (2-Signature Flow) ==

note over Init, Squads #PaleGreen
  **The blockchain is the secure data transport layer.**
  Initiator's signature (Sign 1) is harmless — it only pins
  a proposal to a PDA. No funds move, no programs upgrade.
  Approvers independently fetch, verify, and sign (Sign 2).
end note

' --- Sign 1: Initiator proposes (harmless) ---
Init -> UI: Draft protocol action
note right of UI: Even if UI is compromised, the worst\noutcome is a **malicious proposal on-chain**.\nNo execution. No fund movement.\nCost: ~0.002 SOL rent.
UI -> Squads: **Sign 1:** `Squads::CreateTransaction`\n(Initiator pays rent, proposal stored in PDA)
Squads --> UI: Proposal #45 created\n(Instructions stored on-chain)

' --- OOB hand-off: just a simple number ---
Init -> OOB: "Check Proposal **#45**.\nIntent: Safe Protocol Upgrade"
note over OOB: Just a small integer.\nNo raw bytes. No Base64.\nHuman-readable and verifiable.

' --- Approver 1: independent verify + sign ---
OOB -> Ap1: Receives intent + Index #45
Ap1 -> HW: Input Index #45
HW -> RPC: Fetch Proposal PDA account data for Index #45
RPC --> HW: Raw serialised instruction bytes
note over HW
  **Firmware-Level Decode (Clear Signing)**
  Secure Element deserialises Squads V4 instructions.
  Trusted screen displays human-readable intent.
end note
HW -> Ap1: Screen: "Target: <program_id>"\n"Action: Upgrade Program"\n"Buffer: <verified_hash>"
Ap1 -> HW: Confirms intent matches OOB → **Sign 2**
HW --> RPC: Broadcast `ApproveTransaction`
RPC -> Squads: Approval recorded (1/3)

' --- Approver 2: fully independent, async ---
OOB -> Ap2: Same message: "Check Proposal #45"
note over Ap2: **Async & Independent.**\nNo relay from Ap1 needed.\nAp2 fetches the same PDA\ndirectly from blockchain.
Ap2 -> HW: Input Index #45
HW -> RPC: Fetch same Proposal PDA
RPC --> HW: Same raw bytes
HW -> Ap2: Same decoded intent on screen
Ap2 -> HW: Confirms → **Sign 2**
HW --> RPC: Broadcast `ApproveTransaction`
RPC -> Squads: Approval recorded (2/3)

' --- Approver 3: threshold reached ---
OOB -> Ap3: Same message: "Check Proposal #45"
Ap3 -> HW: Input Index #45
HW -> RPC: Fetch same Proposal PDA
RPC --> HW: Same raw bytes
HW -> Ap3: Same decoded intent on screen
Ap3 -> HW: Confirms → **Sign 2**
HW --> RPC: Broadcast `ApproveTransaction`
RPC -> Squads: Approval recorded (3/3)\n**Threshold reached!**

note over Squads
  Squads V4 marks proposal as Approved.
  Timelock begins (e.g., 72h for Tier 1).
  Watchtowers monitor for revocation window.
end note

== Why the 2-Signature Flow Wins ==

note over Init, Squads
  **Sign 1 (Initiator → CreateTransaction):**
  • Harmless: only pins a draft to the blockchain
  • No execution authority — just paying ~0.002 SOL rent
  • Enables the blockchain to act as **secure data transport**

  **Sign 2 (Each Approver → ApproveTransaction):**
  • Each approver independently queries the same PDA
  • HW Wallet fetches raw bytes via RPC using a simple index
  • Firmware decodes to human-readable intent (Clear Signing)
  • No relay chain between approvers — fully async

  **What the on-chain proposal gives you:**
  1. **Decodeability:** HW fetches full bytes from PDA, not a hash
  2. **Clean transport:** OOB carries "Index #45", not raw bytecode
  3. **Size limit solved:** Instructions stored in PDA, not packed in TX
  4. **Async M-of-N:** Each approver votes independently via blockchain
  5. **Auditability:** Proposal + all votes permanently on-chain
end note

@enduml
